# Build output and local tool state. None of this is source, and tracking it has
# already cost us twice: a half-committed DirectionsActivity (the .java landed,
# its layout did not, and main would not compile from a clean clone), and a
# one-file mode fix that swept in 149 unrelated artifacts.
#
# These files stay on disk -- this only stops git following them.

# Android
rideiq-android/build/
rideiq-android/app/build/
rideiq-android/.gradle/
rideiq-android/local.properties
*.apk
*.aab

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Transit engine working data (GTFS, OSM extracts, the OTP jar, graph.obj).
# rideiq-backend/transit/.gitignore covers this too; repeated here so a clone
# that only reads the root file still gets it right.
rideiq-backend/transit/data/

# Local runtime state
rideiq-backend/rideiq.db
rideiq-backend/cache/

# Trained challenger models and the request log. Both are runtime state that
# differs per deployment: challenger.joblib is produced by retrain.py from
# whatever outcomes that host has collected, and rideiq.db IS those outcomes.
# Committing either would ship one machine's data to every other one.
rideiq-backend/challenger.joblib
rideiq-backend/rideiq.db
rideiq-backend/rideiq.db-wal
rideiq-backend/rideiq.db-shm
